                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="16658050" author="pavel.petroshenko" created="Sun, 21 Oct 2018 02:13:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/5043&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/5043&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16658102" author="pavel.petroshenko" created="Sun, 21 Oct 2018 06:33:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Please give the current patch a look. All my tests seem to work well now.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;BTW Ignite&apos;s Date supports only millions &lt;a href=&quot;https://apacheignite.readme.io/docs/binary-client-protocol-data-format#section-date,&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://apacheignite.readme.io/docs/binary-client-protocol-data-format#section-date,&lt;/a&gt;&#160;so you shouldn&apos;t expect it to work with micros or nanos. Please let me know if I&apos;m missing something.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16658153" author="alexey.kosenchuk" created="Sun, 21 Oct 2018 09:28:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Also, please note, PHP platform&apos;s DateTime (&lt;a href=&quot;http://php.net/manual/en/class.datetime.php)&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://php.net/manual/en/class.datetime.php)&lt;/a&gt; does not support nanoseconds, but only microseconds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That&apos;s why Timestamp::fromDateTime() cannot take nanoseconds from datetime.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16658202" author="pavel.petroshenko" created="Sun, 21 Oct 2018 12:29:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I believe some tests need to be added before it&apos;s merged.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16658790" author="isapego" created="Mon, 22 Oct 2018 09:48:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pavel.petroshenko&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pavel.petroshenko&quot;&gt;pavel.petroshenko&lt;/a&gt; agree, we need tests, if we can implement them here.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16658874" author="spilschikov" created="Mon, 22 Oct 2018 10:46:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pavel.petroshenko&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pavel.petroshenko&quot;&gt;pavel.petroshenko&lt;/a&gt; tested case with Date, now i&apos;ts works&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But with timestamp i still can&apos;t understand&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PHP put&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
$cache = $client-&amp;gt;getOrCreateCache(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;PH_TIMESTAMP&quot;&lt;/span&gt;)-&amp;gt;setKeyType(ObjectType::TIMESTAMP)-&amp;gt;setValueType(ObjectType::INTEGER);
$cache-&amp;gt;put((&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; Timestamp((DateTime::createFromFormat(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;Y-m-d H:i:s.u&apos;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;2018-10-22 13:35:19.117530&apos;&lt;/span&gt;))-&amp;gt;getTimestamp() * 1000, 117530)),1);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;JS get&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
cache = (await igniteClient.getOrCreateCache(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;PH_TIMESTAMP&quot;&lt;/span&gt;)).setKeyType(ObjectType.PRIMITIVE_TYPE.TIMESTAMP);
console.log(JSON.stringify(await cache.get(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; Timestamp(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; Date(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;2018-10-22T13:35:19.117530&apos;&lt;/span&gt;).getTime(), 117530))));
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When using timestamp as key i can&apos;t get value stored with php client (same python). And in a different way, when i put key timestamp from js i can&apos;t get it from php&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But when i put timestamp key from js i can get it with&#160;python&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As you see i using custom Timestamp object and define time and nano seconds&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What should i do to&#160;get same timestamp&#160;in JS or Python?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16658898" author="alexey.kosenchuk" created="Mon, 22 Oct 2018 11:23:56 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=spilschikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;spilschikov&quot;&gt;spilschikov&lt;/a&gt; , you need to update your example for Timestamp.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1) `DateTime-&amp;gt;getTimestamp()&apos; returns the Unix timestamp (&lt;a href=&quot;http://php.net/manual/en/datetime.gettimestamp.php&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://php.net/manual/en/datetime.gettimestamp.php&lt;/a&gt;) i.e. seconds only. So, you lose milliseconds here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2) The nanoseconds part of the Ignite Timestamp contains not all nanoseconds but a nanoseconds fraction of a last millisecond (&lt;a href=&quot;https://apacheignite.readme.io/docs/binary-client-protocol-data-format#section-timestamp&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://apacheignite.readme.io/docs/binary-client-protocol-data-format#section-timestamp&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A correct code would look something like this for your concrete numbers:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;`$cache-&amp;gt;put((new Timestamp((DateTime::createFromFormat(&apos;Y-m-d H:i:s.u&apos;, &apos;2018-10-22 13:35:19.117530&apos;))-&amp;gt;getTimestamp() * 1000 + 117, 530000)),1);`&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes, it looks a bit crazy but this is how Timestamp is defined in the Ignite Binary protocol and which methods PHP&apos;s DateTime provides.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would recommend first to check that everything is fine when you use Timestamp as a value. And only after that, when you use it as a key.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16658912" author="alexey.kosenchuk" created="Mon, 22 Oct 2018 11:50:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;BTW, you should get the exactly same result if you create Timestamp for your concrete time as&lt;br/&gt;
Timestamp::fromDateTime(DateTime::createFromFormat(&apos;Y-m-d H:i:s.u&apos;, &apos;2018-10-22 13:35:19.117530&apos;)))&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because your example-time is defined with the microseconds accuracy, not nanoseconds.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16658924" author="spilschikov" created="Mon, 22 Oct 2018 12:12:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alexey.kosenchuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alexey.kosenchuk&quot;&gt;alexey.kosenchuk&lt;/a&gt; Yeah, looks not so pretty, but it really works, Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
$cache-&amp;gt;put((&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; Timestamp((DateTime::createFromFormat(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;Y-m-d H:i:s.u&apos;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;2018-10-22 13:35:19.117530&apos;&lt;/span&gt;))-&amp;gt;getTimestamp() * 1000 + 117, 117530)),1);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nano seconds stay where they are and we just add millis&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For me all issues are fixed&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16658926" author="spilschikov" created="Mon, 22 Oct 2018 12:13:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;And yes, i note that in nanos i use millis, thanks&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16659078" author="isapego" created="Mon, 22 Oct 2018 15:19:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pavel.petroshenko&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pavel.petroshenko&quot;&gt;pavel.petroshenko&lt;/a&gt;, so, what about tests?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16660093" author="pavel.petroshenko" created="Tue, 23 Oct 2018 05:16:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Tests are ready. Please review and merge.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16660419" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 23 Oct 2018 10:39:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user asfgit closed the pull request at:&lt;/p&gt;

